# mutgap2_rdec_depth_stencil_resolve: Depth and stencil resolves of a 4-sample memoryless depth-stencil attachment into 1-sample private D32S8 textures P and Q, each read back by a later pass that loads it: a red draw at depth 0.5 with depth Less shows whether the depth is the resolved 1.0 (drawn) or the 0.3 stored before (not); stencil Equal shows 3 (resolved) or 5 (stored before). Resolved: depth through the pass descriptor's resolve texture; depth stored Unknown on the memoryless attachment (kept), then 0x69 SetDepthStoreAction MultisampleResolve, or 0x6a (which dispatches to the same decoder); without either nothing is resolved; 0x97 SetDepthResolveTexture moves the resolve from P to Q; stencil stored Unknown (kept), then 0x78 MultisampleResolve; 0x98 SetStencilResolveTexture moves the stencil resolve to Q.
